[
  {
    "text": "India's tectonic plate",
    "start": 0.093458,
    "end": 1.369999
  },
  {
    "text": "is pushing under Tibet.",
    "start": 1.530375,
    "end": 2.806916
  },
  {
    "text": "But the weird part",
    "start": 3.084125,
    "end": 3.936916
  },
  {
    "text": "is what may be\nhappening underneath.",
    "start": 3.936916,
    "end": 5.680749
  },
  {
    "text": "That slow collision helps",
    "start": 5.934583,
    "end": 7.219625
  },
  {
    "text": "build the Himalayas.",
    "start": 7.219625,
    "end": 8.449457
  },
  {
    "text": "Now, a twenty\ntwenty-five seismic study",
    "start": 8.70325,
    "end": 10.8645
  },
  {
    "text": "suggests something deeper:",
    "start": 10.8645,
    "end": 12.526541
  },
  {
    "text": "parts of the\nplate's mantle layer",
    "start": 12.93225,
    "end": 14.325625
  },
  {
    "text": "may be tearing and peeling away",
    "start": 14.357458,
    "end": 16.436916
  },
  {
    "text": "from its crust.",
    "start": 16.436916,
    "end": 17.304583
  },
  {
    "text": "That's inferred from\nseismic evidence,",
    "start": 17.558416,
    "end": 19.430708
  },
  {
    "text": "not a surface split.",
    "start": 19.56775,
    "end": 20.704083
  },
  {
    "text": "The country isn't disappearing.",
    "start": 20.94625,
    "end": 22.561582
  },
  {
    "text": "Those enormous mountains",
    "start": 22.827083,
    "end": 24.030375
  },
  {
    "text": "are just the surface",
    "start": 24.030375,
    "end": 25.070083
  },
  {
    "text": "of a much bigger collision.",
    "start": 25.070083,
    "end": 26.743832
  }
]
